    <h2 id="vpn">VPNs — The Encrypted Tunnels</h2>

    <h3>What is a VPN?</h3>
    <p>A <strong>Virtual Private Network (VPN)</strong> creates an encrypted, private "tunnel" through a public network
      (like the Internet). Data traveling through this tunnel is encrypted, so even if it is intercepted, it cannot be
      read without the decryption key. VPNs allow remote users and branch offices to securely communicate with a central
      network as if they were physically connected to it.</p>

    <div class="callout analogy">
      <div class="callout-title">📦 The Armored Truck Analogy</div>
      Sending data over the Internet without a VPN is like sending valuables in a glass truck — everyone can see what's
      inside. A VPN is like an armored truck with tinted windows and a coded lock — it travels the same public roads
      (the Internet), but no one can see or steal what's inside.
    </div>

    <h3>How a VPN Works</h3>
    <div class="step-flow">
      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>VPN Client Initiates Connection</strong>
          <p>Your device runs a VPN client (app or built-in OS feature). It contacts the VPN server and begins a
            handshake to establish a secure connection.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Authentication</strong>
          <p>Both ends verify each other's identity — using certificates, pre-shared keys, or username/password
            credentials. This prevents connecting to a rogue VPN server.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Tunnel Establishment &amp; Key Exchange</strong>
          <p>A shared encryption key is negotiated (using algorithms like Diffie-Hellman). An encrypted "tunnel" is
            created — all subsequent traffic travels inside this tunnel.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Data Encapsulation &amp; Encryption</strong>
          <p>Your data packets are wrapped (encapsulated) in another packet with VPN headers, then encrypted using
            AES-256 or similar. The original source/destination is hidden.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num">5</div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <strong>Decryption at Destination</strong>
          <p>The VPN server at the other end decrypts the packet, strips the outer wrapping, and forwards the original
            data to its intended destination inside the secure network.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

