      WireGuard, released in 2019, has only ~4,000 lines of code compared to OpenVPN's ~400,000. This smaller codebase
      means fewer vulnerabilities, easier auditing, and significantly better performance. It is now the default protocol
      in many major VPN providers and Linux kernels 5.6+.
    </div>

    <div class="pros-cons">
      <div class="pros">
        <h4>✅ VPN Advantages</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Strong data encryption in transit</li>
          <li>Hides source IP and bypasses geo-blocks</li>
          <li>Enables secure remote work</li>
          <li>Protects traffic on public Wi-Fi</li>
          <li>Site-to-site connectivity for branches</li>
