    <p>In a well-designed enterprise network, these controls work in concert. A remote employee authenticates through
      MFA (access control), connects via VPN (encrypted tunnel), passes through the corporate firewall (perimeter
      control), and all their activity is monitored by the IPS. If their device is compromised, behavioral anomalies are
      caught by IDS before an attacker can pivot deeper into the network.</p>

